  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the 2017 image as a target of judgment",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the 2017 image of the Black woman walking in a revealing outfit, as the meme's text '2017... terribly right' frames her as the subject of negative judgment. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the rhetorical structure of the meme positions the viewer as someone who is meant to accept or internalize the negative evaluation of the 2017 scene, thereby projecting the user's identity onto the scene as the recipient of the meme's moral condemnation.",
